 "wu_crossover_run": "Cross over long, do not hop. One rep is one full run over the distance shown, at the effort shown.",
 "wu_crossover_symmetry_full_warmup": "You need: resistance bands and secure band anchor. Stand facing the anchor, feet hip-width, a big step back so the bands are taut at the start. Do all 7 movements in order, 10 smooth reps each as a warm-up (light bands) (exhale on every pull): 1) Row — bands at chest height, standing tall: pull the handles to your ribs, pinching the shoulder blades together. 2) Reverse Fly — bands at chest height, arms straight in front: open the arms out to a T, squeezing the upper back and rear shoulders. 3) Pulldown — bands at the high anchor, slight forward lean: pull straight arms down to your hips, shoulders down and back. 4) 90/90 External Rotation — bands at shoulder height, elbows up at shoulder level and bent 90°: rotate the forearms up and back without moving the elbows. 5) Scaption — bands at the low anchor, standing tall: raise straight arms to shoulder height at 45° (a Y-shape in front of you), thumbs up. 6) Incline Plus — bands at the low anchor behind you, leaning forward like an incline plank: press the arms forward and push the shoulder blades apart at the end. 7) Victory — bands at the low anchor, core braced: press up and back into a wide overhead V finish without arching the low back. One round is all 7 movements, done back to back.",
